{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtMvzNBAtCzCGkLn1BgS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've added the `codex-sandboxed` lane: `./run.sh <task> codex-sandboxed [rep]`. I tested it only with a stub `codex`; a real Codex run hasn't happened yet because it would call OpenAI.\n\nThe lane runs exactly the same `codex exec` command as the `codex` lane, set up the way the kimi lane is:\n- It gets an empty scratch HOME with `CODEX_HOME` inside it, deleted after the run. Codex logs in with `CODEX_API_KEY` from the environment and is installed under `/opt/homebrew`, so it doesn't need anything from the real home.\n- It runs inside `sandbox-exec -f sandbox/agent.sb`.\n\nThree things had to differ from a straight copy:\n1. **`final.txt` is copied out at the end.** Per the README, the run folder lives under the real home on the eval Mac (`~/evals/agent-evals/runs/...`), so Codex can't write it from inside the sandbox. Codex writes `final.txt` to the scratch HOME and `run.sh` copies it into the run folder afterwards. `agent.log` and `agent.err` are unaffected, because bash opens those before the sandbox starts.\n2. **Codex's own sandbox stays off.** It can't run inside `sandbox-exec`, so `agent.sb` is the only fence, same as for kimi.\n3. **I changed `sandbox/agent.sb`.** It always allowed `~/.kimi-code`, which would have let Codex read Kimi's install, config and sessions. The folder it allows is now passed in as `-D AGENT_DIR=`. The kimi lane passes `~/.kimi-code`, so it behaves as before; the Codex lane passes its scratch HOME, so nothing in the real home is open to it.\n\n**Testing:**\n- `codex --version` works under the profile.\n- With the stub, the agent could not read `~/.codex/config.toml`, `~/.zshrc` or `~/.kimi-code`, and could not write to the home.\n- Writing to the task folder and to the scratch `CODEX_HOME` worked, and `final.txt` came through to `answer.json`.\n- The kimi lane can still open `~/.kimi-code` and still can't read `~/.zshrc`.\n\n**Limits:**\n- Like the kimi lane, the profile still lets the agent check whether a path it already knows exists and see its size. It can't read file contents or list folders.\n- For the first real run, try `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed`. If it fails, `agent.err` should show what Codex wanted from the home folder.\n\nI also updated the lane lists in `README.md` and the `run.sh` header, and wrote it all up in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_read_input_tokens":33643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":341},"output_tokens":801,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60e28c5b-2fe8-4676-aa78-df7cf73b50fd","uuid":"ab938501-71a8-483e-87ec-cc315fe52885","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:14:48.705Z","request_id":"req_011CgtMvzEUsEFhuaj7dKM6D"}
